 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“In this outward and physical ceremony we attest once again to the inner and spiritual strength of our Nation. As my high school teacher, Miss Julia Coleman, used to say: ‘We must adjust to changing times and still hold to unchanging principles.’ . . .</p>\n<p>This inauguration ceremony marks a new beginning, a new dedication within our Government, and a new spirit among us all. A President may sense and proclaim that new spirit, but only a people can provide it.</p>\n<p>Two centuries ago our Nation's birth was a milestone in the long quest for freedom, but the bold and brilliant dream which excited the founders of this Nation still awaits its consummation. I have no new dream to set forth today, but rather urge a fresh faith in the old dream.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Jimmy Carter, First Inaugural Address, January 20, 1977</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 616814,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following best describes the context surrounding the excerpted speech?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1174479,
     "content_html": "An economic crisis was over but the nation was still looking for new leadership."
    },
    {
     "id": 1174480,
     "content_html": "People had lost trust in their government and elected a president who was an outsider."
    },
    {
     "id": 1174478,
     "content_html": "The nation had recently won a controversial war and was on the path toward healing."
    },
    {
     "id": 1174477,
     "content_html": "The strengthening Civil Rights movement was uniting the United States."
    }
   ],
